	"thethTitle": "Thethi",
	"thethSubTitle": "The Alpine Sanctuary",
	"thethRegionTitle": "Shkod\u00ebr, Albania",
	"thethArtifactCulture": "Albanian Highland",
	"thethArtifactGeolocation": "Northern Albania",
	"thethPullQuote1Top": "A Living Fragment of",
	"thethPullQuote1Bottom": "Europe's Last Wilderness",
	"thethPullQuote1Author": "Edith Durham",
	"thethPullQuote2": "The Albanian Alps are perhaps the last great wilderness in Europe, a place where time seems to have stood still.",
	"thethPullQuote2Author": "Edith Durham",
	"thethCallout1": "Thethi's iconic Lock-in Tower (Kulla e Ngujimit) was used as a refuge for men involved in blood feuds under the Kanun of L\u00ebk\u00eb Dukagjini, the traditional Albanian code of law.",
	"thethCallout2": "The Thethi valley sits at approximately 2,500 feet (760 m) above sea level, surrounded by peaks exceeding 8,000 feet (2,500 m), including the dramatic Radohima massif.",
	"thethVideoCaption": "\u201cThethi National Park - Albania's Hidden Alpine Paradise.\u201d Youtube.",
	"thethMapCaption": "Map showing location of Thethi in the Albanian Alps, northern Albania.",
	"thethHistoryInfo1": "Thethi is a remote alpine village nestled in a glacial valley in the Albanian Alps (Bjeshk\u00ebt e Nemuna), in the Shkod\u00ebr district of northern Albania. The valley has been inhabited for centuries by Albanian highland clans, who maintained a fiercely independent way of life governed by the Kanun, a set of customary laws attributed to L\u00ebk\u00eb Dukagjini.\nThe isolation of the valley \u2014 accessible only by mountain passes for most of its history \u2014 preserved a traditional way of life largely unchanged until the 20th century.",
	"thethHistoryInfo2": "During the communist period (1944-1991), the Albanian government attempted to modernize the highlands, building roads and schools but also restricting traditional customs. After the fall of communism, many highland villages were depopulated as residents moved to lowland cities.\nIn recent years, Thethi has experienced a revival as a destination for hiking and ecotourism, with the Peaks of the Balkans trail bringing international attention to the region's natural beauty and cultural heritage.",
	"thethConstructionInfo1": "Thethi's traditional stone houses (sht\u00ebpi) are built from local limestone and timber, designed to withstand harsh mountain winters. The houses typically feature thick stone walls, small windows to conserve heat, and wooden balconies. Stone-slab roofs, anchored with heavy rocks, protect against the heavy snowfall that blankets the valley for several months each year.\nThe most famous structure in Thethi is the Lock-in Tower (Kulla e Ngujimit), a stone tower used historically as a place of refuge for men targeted in blood feuds.",
	"thethConstructionInfo2": "The Church of Thethi (Kisha e Thethit), built in the 19th century, is a small but picturesque stone church set against the dramatic mountain backdrop. Traditional highland architecture throughout the valley includes watermills along the Thethi River, stone bridges, and livestock enclosures built with dry-stone walling techniques passed down through generations.",
	"thethLocationInfo1": "Thethi lies within the Thethi National Park, established in 1966, covering approximately 5,200 acres (2,100 hectares) of pristine alpine wilderness. The valley is surrounded by the peaks of the Albanian Alps, including Radohima at 8,146 feet (2,568 m) and Haj-Nehaj at 8,524 feet (2,598 m).",
	"thethLocationInfo2": "The Blue Eye of Thethi (Syri i Kalt\u00ebr), a stunning natural spring pool of vivid turquoise water, is one of the valley's most remarkable natural features. The Grunas Waterfall, cascading 100 feet (30 m) down a limestone cliff, is another iconic landmark. The valley connects to Valbona via a popular mountain pass trek at approximately 5,900 feet (1,800 m).",
	"theth1438ce": "Albanian highland clans are well established in the Thethi valley, governed by the Kanun of L\u00ebk\u00eb Dukagjini",
	"theth1572ce": "The highland communities resist Ottoman control, maintaining autonomy through the rugged terrain of the Albanian Alps",
	"theth1867ce": "British traveler and diplomat Edith Durham visits the Albanian highlands, later documenting the traditional way of life in her celebrated writings",
	"theth1911ce": "Albania declares independence in 1912; the highland regions play a crucial role in the national awakening and resistance movements",
	"theth1964ce": "Thethi National Park is established in 1966, one of Albania's first protected areas, preserving the alpine ecosystem",
	"theth1997ce": "The Peaks of the Balkans trail is inaugurated, connecting Albania, Kosovo, and Montenegro and bringing renewed international attention to Thethi",
