	"krujaTitle": "Kruj\u00eb",
	"krujaSubTitle": "The Fortress of Skanderbeg",
	"krujaRegionTitle": "Durr\u00ebs County, Albania",
	"krujaArtifactCulture": "Medieval Albanian",
	"krujaArtifactGeolocation": "Central Albania",
	"krujaPullQuote1Top": "The Shield of Christendom",
	"krujaPullQuote1Bottom": "Against the Ottoman Tide",
	"krujaPullQuote1Author": "Pope Callixtus III",
	"krujaPullQuote2": "Skanderbeg's defense of Kruj\u00eb is one of the most remarkable episodes of resistance in European military history.",
	"krujaPullQuote2Author": "Fan Noli",
	"krujaCallout1": "Gjergj Kastrioti Skanderbeg successfully defended Kruj\u00eb against three major Ottoman sieges, earning him the title \"Athleta Christi\" (Champion of Christ) from the Pope.",
	"krujaCallout2": "The castle sits at an elevation of approximately 1,970 feet (600 m) atop the Skanderbeg Mountain (Mali i Sariut), providing a commanding view of the surrounding plains.",
	"krujaVideoCaption": "\u201cKruj\u00eb Castle and the Legacy of Skanderbeg - Albania.\u201d Youtube.",
	"krujaMapCaption": "Map showing location of Kruj\u00eb in central Albania.",
	"krujaHistoryInfo1": "Kruj\u00eb is a city in north-central Albania, historically renowned as the seat of Gjergj Kastrioti Skanderbeg (1405-1468), Albania's national hero. The castle of Kruj\u00eb has been fortified since at least the 5th century and became the capital of the Principality of Kastrioti in the 15th century.\nIn 1443, Skanderbeg raised the Albanian flag over the castle after abandoning his forced service in the Ottoman army, beginning a 25-year campaign of resistance against the Ottoman Empire.",
	"krujaHistoryInfo2": "Skanderbeg successfully defended Kruj\u00eb against three major Ottoman sieges \u2014 in 1450, 1466, and 1467 \u2014 each time repelling vastly superior forces. His resistance prevented Ottoman expansion into Western Europe for decades and earned him admiration across the Christian world.\nAfter Skanderbeg's death in 1468, the castle fell to the Ottomans in 1478 after a prolonged fourth siege. The city remained under Ottoman control until Albanian independence in 1912.",
	"krujaConstructionInfo1": "The Kruj\u00eb Castle is perched on a rocky outcrop at the edge of Skanderbeg Mountain (Mali i Sariut). The fortress walls follow the natural contours of the terrain, encircling an area that once contained a small town with houses, churches, and a bazaar.\nThe Skanderbeg Museum, designed by architects Pranvera Hoxha and Pirro Vaso and opened in 1982, sits within the castle walls. Built in a modernist style inspired by medieval Albanian architecture, it houses artifacts from the period of Albanian resistance.",
	"krujaConstructionInfo2": "Below the castle, the restored Old Bazaar (Pazari i Vjet\u00ebr) stretches along a cobblestone street with traditional stone and timber shops. The bazaar has been in continuous use since the 15th century and today sells traditional Albanian crafts, antiques, and locally made goods. The Dollma Tekke, a small Bektashi shrine within the castle complex, features elegant Ottoman-era architecture with painted interiors.",
	"krujaLocationInfo1": "Kruj\u00eb is located approximately 20 miles (32 km) north of Tirana in central Albania. The castle sits atop a mountain spur overlooking the vast western Albanian plain that stretches to the Adriatic Sea, providing strategic visibility over approaching forces \u2014 a key factor in Skanderbeg's successful defense.",
	"krujaLocationInfo2": "The Skanderbeg Mountain (Mali i Sariut) rises steeply behind the castle to approximately 3,500 feet (1,070 m). The surrounding terrain of steep gorges and dense forests provided natural defensive advantages that Skanderbeg exploited in his guerrilla tactics against the much larger Ottoman forces. The nearby Sarisalltiku peak features a cave shrine venerated by both Muslims and Christians.",
	"kruja1200bce": "Early Illyrian settlements exist in the Kruj\u00eb region, taking advantage of the natural fortress position",
	"kruja106bce": "The region falls under Roman control as part of the province of Illyricum",
	"kruja551ce": "Byzantine-era fortifications are constructed on the hilltop, establishing the castle as a strategic defensive position",
	"kruja1812ce": "The castle ruins and old bazaar are documented by European travelers as interest in Albanian history grows",
	"kruja1958ce": "The Skanderbeg Museum within the castle is established, becoming Albania's most important national memorial",
	"kruja1989ce": "Kruj\u00eb becomes a major tourist destination and symbol of Albanian national identity after the fall of communism",
