	"korcaTitle": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb",
	"korcaSubTitle": "The Cradle of Albanian Culture",
	"korcaRegionTitle": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb, Albania",
	"korcaArtifactCulture": "Albanian Orthodox",
	"korcaArtifactGeolocation": "Southeastern Albania",
	"korcaPullQuote1Top": "Not Just a Cathedral,",
	"korcaPullQuote1Bottom": "but the Soul of a Nation",
	"korcaPullQuote1Author": "Fan Noli",
	"korcaPullQuote2": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb is the city where Albanian national consciousness first found its voice through schools, literature, and art.",
	"korcaPullQuote2Author": "Faik Konica",
	"korcaCallout1": "The Resurrection Cathedral (Katedralja Ngjallja e Krishtit) is the largest Orthodox cathedral in Albania, designed by renowned architect Fan Noli and completed in 2003.",
	"korcaCallout2": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb is home to the first Albanian-language school, opened on March 7, 1887, a date now celebrated as Teacher's Day (Dita e M\u00ebsuesit) across Albania.",
	"korcaVideoCaption": "\u201cKor\u00e7\u00eb - The Cradle of Albanian Culture and the Resurrection Cathedral.\u201d Youtube.",
	"korcaMapCaption": "Map showing location of Kor\u00e7\u00eb in southeastern Albania.",
	"korcaHistoryInfo1": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb is a city in southeastern Albania, situated in a high plateau at approximately 2,800 feet (850 m) above sea level. The city has been a center of Albanian culture, education, and art since the 19th century, earning it the title \"the cradle of Albanian culture.\"\nThe first Albanian-language school was opened here on March 7, 1887, by Pandeli Sotiri, marking a pivotal moment in the Albanian national awakening. Kor\u00e7\u00eb also hosted the first Albanian printing press and numerous literary societies.",
	"korcaHistoryInfo2": "The original Orthodox Cathedral was destroyed during the communist period when Albania declared itself the world's first atheist state in 1967, demolishing nearly all religious buildings. The new Resurrection Cathedral (Katedralja Ngjallja e Krishtit) was built between 1992 and 2003 on the foundations of the old cathedral, symbolizing both religious revival and national cultural renewal.\nKor\u00e7\u00eb is also renowned for its contribution to Albanian music, art, and the famous annual Kor\u00e7\u00eb Beer Festival, one of the largest in the Balkans.",
	"korcaConstructionInfo1": "The Resurrection Cathedral was designed in a neo-Byzantine style, drawing inspiration from traditional Orthodox church architecture while incorporating modern construction techniques. The cathedral features a cruciform plan with a large central dome reaching approximately 100 feet (30 m) in height, flanked by smaller domes.\nThe exterior is clad in light-colored stone with decorative arched windows, while the interior is adorned with frescoes and iconography painted by Albanian and Greek artists.",
	"korcaConstructionInfo2": "The cathedral's construction spanned over a decade, from 1992 to 2003. Modern reinforced concrete and steel frame construction was used for structural integrity, while traditional stone and decorative elements maintain the Byzantine aesthetic.\nThe bell tower, rising beside the cathedral, houses a set of bells that ring across the city. The surrounding plaza and park create a cultural center for the city, connecting to the National Museum of Medieval Art, which houses one of the finest collections of Byzantine icons in the world.",
	"korcaLocationInfo1": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb is located in the Kor\u00e7\u00eb Basin, a fertile plateau surrounded by mountains in southeastern Albania. The city lies approximately 112 miles (180 km) southeast of Tirana, near the borders with both Greece and North Macedonia. The Morava Mountain range rises to the east, while Lake Ohrid lies to the northeast.",
	"korcaLocationInfo2": "The Kor\u00e7\u00eb plateau has been inhabited since prehistoric times due to its fertile soil and strategic position along ancient trade routes connecting the Adriatic and Aegean seas. The nearby archaeological site of Maliq, on the shores of a former lake, has yielded evidence of continuous habitation dating back to the Neolithic period, around 6000 BCE.",
	"korca1631ce": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb develops as an Ottoman administrative and trade center with construction of mosques, bazaars, and hans (inns)",
	"korca1647ce": "The city's importance grows as a crossroads of trade routes connecting Thessaloniki, Ioannina, and the Albanian coast",
	"korca1658ce": "Cultural and religious communities flourish in Kor\u00e7\u00eb, establishing it as a multi-ethnic center of learning",
	"korca1901ce": "Kor\u00e7\u00eb becomes a center of the Albanian national movement with the opening of the first Albanian-language school in 1887",
	"korca1984ce": "During the communist era, the original Orthodox Cathedral and most religious buildings are demolished as Albania is declared an atheist state",
	"korca1998ce": "Construction of the new Resurrection Cathedral begins after the fall of communism, completed in 2003 as a symbol of cultural renewal",
